  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday morning through next Saturday)\nIssued at 201 PM EDT Sun Sep 13 2026\n\nThe extended period begins Tue with an upper ridge centered over the \nGA/TN/NC borders along with a surface ridge/wedge nosing down the \neastern seaboard from the New England states. By Tue morning the \nwedge will be firmly entrenched into North and Central GA with Eats \nto SE winds in the 8-12mph range. We will still have decent moisture \nacross the area Tues as the drier airmass does not really start to \nmove in until Wed. With the ridge/wedge building in we could still \nsee a shower or two mainly across east central GA but not expecting \nmuch. As that drier air filters into the region Wed we will see \nDewpoints drop into the low to middle 60s and continuing across the \nstate through the end of the week. High temps stay in the upper 80s \nto lower 90s through the end of the week but with the drier air \nmoving in  Heat Index values will drop from the upper 902 to lower \n100s Tue to the lower 90s Wed to Fri. \n\nModels show moisture beginning to return Fri evening into Sat as the \nridge finally begins to break down. The continued east to \nsoutheasterly flow brings atlantic moisture in across the state as \nwe get into the weekend. Right now just going with a 20% to 30% \nchance of showers and thunderstorms Sat/Sun.",
